{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/skills/using-qualifier/SKILL.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:16:51.817364Z","id":"d99acfab215cf6ef3ddeda4fcd36e5b8b5ec123b089ff29068987ddce87411fd","body":{"detail":"All nine SKILL.md files have `allowed-tools: Bash(qualifier:*), ...` on line 4, and scripts/test-plugin.sh:1095 requires it. The skills write `qualifier` \"for short\" (using-qualifier/SKILL.md:87-89), so a model that copies an example literally runs the bare command. With this rule the command runs without a prompt. If a `qualifier` of another version is on PATH, it silently writes records with a CLI the skills were not checked against. If none is on PATH, the call fails with command-not-found. Both outcomes contradict the plugin's own contract: ensure-qualifier.sh:3-4 says \"A `qualifier` on PATH is never probed, used, or modified\", and session-start:131 says a PATH qualifier \"is not used and may be a different version\". The pre-approval rewards the one call form the plugin calls wrong.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":4},"end":{"line":4},"content_hash":"4373d05fe09edc66de2ed4867e42003f1fb70409b19eb469632f674b0b622d46"},"suggested_fix":"Either drop `Bash(qualifier:*)` from every skill's allowed-tools (and from the required list at scripts/test-plugin.sh:1095), so a bare call at least prompts. Or ship a `bin/qualifier` shim that execs `ensure-qualifier.sh exec \"$@\"`. Files in a plugin's `bin/` are on the Bash tool's PATH (https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins-reference#standard-layout), which makes the bare form the pinned binary. Note that the same docs say claude.ai and Cowork don't install plugins that have a `bin/` directory.","summary":"Every qual skill pre-approves bare `Bash(qualifier:*)`, which auto-approves the PATH qualifier that the plugin says it never uses and that may be a different version","tags":["review","review:2026-10-01","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/skills/using-qualifier/SKILL.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:18:41.780131Z","id":"84881aa7e68ec88385af5cb7abe144b59426ae0260941d0d4554dbb2d8b16b4a","body":{"detail":"`grep -n allowed-tools plugins/claude-code/skills/*/SKILL.md` shows `Bash(qualifier:*)` on line 4 of all nine skills. scripts/test-plugin.sh:1095 requires it. using-qualifier/SKILL.md:87-89 says \"these skills write `qualifier` for short\". plugins/claude-code/scripts/ensure-qualifier.sh:3-4 says \"A `qualifier` on PATH is never probed, used, or modified\". A bare call therefore runs whatever is on PATH without a prompt.","kind":"comment","references":"d99acfab215cf6ef3ddeda4fcd36e5b8b5ec123b089ff29068987ddce87411fd","summary":"confirmed: every qual skill auto-approves bare `qualifier`, which runs the PATH binary that the wrapper says it never uses","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/skills/using-qualifier/SKILL.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:34:02.796881Z","id":"abca7cfe9d7c0da584f44066ff8ebac5af544b870fc7294096cd3df6cf290a1b","body":{"detail":"Option A: drop Bash(qualifier:*) from all nine SKILL.md allowed-tools lines and from scripts/test-plugin.sh:1095, so a bare 'qualifier' call prompts instead of silently running an unpinned PATH binary. Option B: ship plugins/claude-code/bin/qualifier, a shim that runs 'ensure-qualifier.sh exec \"$@\"', making the bare form the pinned binary; per https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins-reference#standard-layout this affects where the plugin can be installed. Recommendation: A; it keeps the pinned-binary guarantee without a new install constraint.","kind":"comment","references":"d99acfab215cf6ef3ddeda4fcd36e5b8b5ec123b089ff29068987ddce87411fd","summary":"Needs a decision: How should the skills' Bash(qualifier:*) allow rule handle a qualifier on PATH?","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/skills/using-qualifier/SKILL.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"human","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:42:59.772990Z","id":"7aa2edd8e5851ef41924aa159367ad4eadae9140dfff453a26f7844990c54f56","body":{"detail":"Drop the rule","kind":"comment","references":"d99acfab215cf6ef3ddeda4fcd36e5b8b5ec123b089ff29068987ddce87411fd","summary":"Decided: drop the Bash(qualifier:*) rule from all nine SKILL.md allowed-tools lines and from scripts/test-plugin.sh:1095, so a bare qualifier call prompts instead of silently running an unpinned PATH binary. No bin/ shim.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/skills/using-qualifier/SKILL.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-02T01:01:03.956728Z","id":"12b8fba757b71e236959984ec8dff019e8849e0a12830761819e1a20b3b48f1b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9d47f29675ced7584e0436ca567091c00e27b4c4","summary":"Fixed in 9d47f296 (fix(plugin): stop pre-approving a bare qualifier on PATH in skills (d99acfab)). `grep -n 'Bash(qualifier' plugins/claude-code/skills/*/SKILL.md` prints nothing; scripts/test-plugin.sh check 'skills: frontmatter, ...' now asserts 'allowed-tools must not pre-approve a bare qualifier on PATH' (fails if the rule is re-added)","supersedes":"d99acfab215cf6ef3ddeda4fcd36e5b8b5ec123b089ff29068987ddce87411fd","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
